arguments.prompt:
Implement a support ticket classifier in the .NET 10 Web API at /tmp/sv-4228b39f2737445087c2da290f1c7021/TicketClassifier.

## Context

The project is a minimal .NET 10 Web API. It has:
- `Program.cs` with a basic `WebApplication` setup using controllers
- `TicketClassifier.csproj` targeting `net10.0`
- `Data/tickets.csv` with columns: Subject, Description, Priority, Category (Billing, Technical, General)

The CSV content:
```
Subject,Description,Priority,Category
"Cannot login","I am unable to login to my account",1,Technical
"Billing error","I was charged twice for my subscription",2,Billing
"How to reset password","I need help resetting my password",3,General
"Server down","The API server is returning 500 errors",1,Technical
"Refund request","I would like a refund for last month",2,Billing
"Feature question","Does the product support SSO?",3,General
```

## Requirements

Use **ML.NET** (`Microsoft.ML`) for multiclass classification. This is structured tabular data — do NOT use an LLM.

### Guardrails from skill guidance:
1. Set random seed: `new MLContext(seed: 42)`
2. Use `TrainTestSplit` — never evaluate on training data
3. Log evaluation metrics (micro/macro accuracy, log-loss)
4. Use `PredictionEnginePool` in ASP.NET Core (not singleton PredictionEngine)
5. Register services via DI

### Implementation plan:

1. **Add NuGet packages** to `.csproj`:
   - `Microsoft.ML` Version `4.*`
   - `Microsoft.Extensions.ML` (for `PredictionEnginePool`)

2. **Create `Models/TicketData.cs`** with:
   ```csharp
   using Microsoft.ML.Data;

   namespace TicketClassifier.Models;

   public class TicketInput
   {
       [LoadColumn(0)]
       public string Subject { get; set; } = "";

       [LoadColumn(1)]
       public string Description { get; set; } = "";

       [LoadColumn(2)]
       public float Priority { get; set; }

       [LoadColumn(3)]
       public string Category { get; set; } = "";
   }

   public class TicketPrediction
   {
       [ColumnName("PredictedLabel")]
       public string Category { get; set; } = "";

       public float[] Score { get; set; } = [];
   }
   ```

3. **Create `Services/ModelTrainerService.cs`** — a hosted service that trains the model at startup, evaluates it, logs metrics, and saves the model to a file path. Key points:
   - Use `IHostedService` (or `BackgroundService`) to train on startup
   - Combine Subject + Description into a single text feature using `CustomMapping` or concatenation
   - Featurize text with `FeaturizeText`
   - Include Priority as a numeric feature
   - Concatenate all features
   - Use `SdcaMaximumEntropy` trainer for multiclass
   - TrainTestSplit with testFraction: 0.2
   - Log MulticlassClassification metrics (MicroAccuracy, MacroAccuracy, LogLoss)
   - Save model to `Data/model.zip`

   ```csharp
   using Microsoft.ML;
   using TicketClassifier.Models;

   namespace TicketClassifier.Services;

   public class ModelTrainerService : IHostedService
   {
       private readonly ILogger<ModelTrainerService> _logger;
       private readonly string _dataPath;
       private readonly string _modelPath;

       public ModelTrainerService(ILogger<ModelTrainerService> logger, IWebHostEnvironment env)
       {
           _logger = logger;
           _dataPath = Path.Combine(env.ContentRootPath, "Data", "tickets.csv");
           _modelPath = Path.Combine(env.ContentRootPath, "Data", "model.zip");
       }

       public Task StartAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
       {
           var mlContext = new MLContext(seed: 42);

           IDataView data = mlContext.Data.LoadFromTextFile<TicketInput>(
               _dataPath, hasHeader: true, separatorChar: ',', allowQuoting: true);

           var split = mlContext.Data.TrainTestSplit(data, testFraction: 0.2);

           var pipeline = mlContext.Transforms.Text.FeaturizeText("SubjectFeaturized", nameof(TicketInput.Subject))
               .Append(mlContext.Transforms.Text.FeaturizeText("DescriptionFeaturized", nameof(TicketInput.Description)))
               .Append(mlContext.Transforms.Concatenate("Features", "SubjectFeaturized", "DescriptionFeaturized", nameof(TicketInput.Priority)))
               .Append(mlContext.Transforms.Conversion.MapValueToKey("Label", nameof(TicketInput.Category)))
               .Append(mlContext.MulticlassClassification.Trainers.SdcaMaximumEntropy("Label", "Features"))
               .Append(mlContext.Transforms.Conversion.MapKeyToValue("PredictedLabel"));

           var model = pipeline.Fit(split.TrainSet);

           var predictions = model.Transform(split.TestSet);
           var metrics = mlContext.MulticlassClassification.Evaluate(predictions);

           _logger.LogInformation("=== Model Evaluation Metrics ===");
           _logger.LogInformation("Micro Accuracy: {MicroAccuracy:F4}", metrics.MicroAccuracy);
           _logger.LogInformation("Macro Accuracy: {MacroAccuracy:F4}", metrics.MacroAccuracy);
           _logger.LogInformation("Log Loss:       {LogLoss:F4}", metrics.LogLoss);
           _logger.LogInformation("Log Loss Reduction: {LogLossReduction:F4}", metrics.LogLossReduction);
           _logger.LogInformation("================================");

           mlContext.Model.Save(model, data.Schema, _modelPath);
           _logger.LogInformation("Model saved to {ModelPath}", _modelPath);

           return Task.CompletedTask;
       }

       public Task StopAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken) => Task.CompletedTask;
   }
   ```

4. **Create `Controllers/TicketController.cs`**:
   ```csharp
   using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
   using Microsoft.Extensions.ML;
   using TicketClassifier.Models;

   namespace TicketClassifier.Controllers;

   [ApiController]
   [Route("api/[controller]")]
   public class TicketController : ControllerBase
   {
       private readonly PredictionEnginePool<TicketInput, TicketPrediction> _predictionPool;

       public TicketController(PredictionEnginePool<TicketInput, TicketPrediction> predictionPool)
       {
           _predictionPool = predictionPool;
       }

       [HttpPost("classify")]
       public ActionResult<TicketPredictionResponse> Classify([FromBody] TicketRequest request)
       {
           var input = new TicketInput
           {
               Subject = request.Subject,
               Description = request.Description,
               Priority = request.Priority,
           };

           var prediction = _predictionPool.Predict(input);

           return Ok(new TicketPredictionResponse
           {
               Category = prediction.Category,
               Confidence = prediction.Score.Max(),
           });
       }
   }

   public class TicketRequest
   {
       public string Subject { get; set; } = "";
       public string Description { get; set; } = "";
       public float Priority { get; set; }
   }

   public class TicketPredictionResponse
   {
       public string Category { get; set; } = "";
       public float Confidence { get; set; }
   }
   ```

5. **Update `Program.cs`**:
   ```csharp
   using Microsoft.Extensions.ML;
   using TicketClassifier.Models;
   using TicketClassifier.Services;

   var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
   builder.Services.AddControllers();

   builder.Services.AddHostedService<ModelTrainerService>();

   var modelPath = Path.Combine(builder.Environment.ContentRootPath, "Data", "model.zip");
   builder.Services.AddPredictionEnginePool<TicketInput, TicketPrediction>()
       .FromFile(modelPath);

   var app = builder.Build();
   app.MapControllers();
   app.Run();
   ```

6. **Update `.csproj`** to add the ML.NET packages and ensure the CSV is copied to output:
   Add PackageReferences for `Microsoft.ML` and `Microsoft.Extensions.ML`, and add an ItemGroup to copy `Data/tickets.csv` as content.

## Instructions

1. Install the NuGet packages first using `dotnet add package`
2. Create all the files listed above
3. Build with `dotnet build` and fix any errors
4. Make sure the build succeeds cleanly

Do NOT create any test projects. Just implement the code and verify it builds.

